WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:03.280
CATTALYYA NUENGSIGKAPIAN: Hello,
I'm Cattalyya Nuengsigkapian.

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:06.540
I am junior studying computer
science and engineering.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:10.690
My project is camera system
for indoor localization

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.170
and human identification.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.600
Smart home technology is
becoming more and more popular,

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.770
since it give people
the power to control

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:23.010
the device in their home,
to detect indoor accidents,

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.920
and to do health analysis.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:29.280
To support this application
with multi-user,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.700
many research try to
differentiate users

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.350
in their system.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:38.910
But it is difficult for them
to achieve both high accuracy

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.570
and comfort at the same time.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:49.760
These system either require user
to carry an extra device, which

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.260
trade-off the comfort, or use
the camera with very detailed

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.140
vision, recognition
[INAUDIBLE] face,

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:04.800
which can be very blurry in the
low resolution cameras or very

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.370
low speed camera in
most civilian system.

00:01:08.370 --> 00:01:13.170
In order to achieve both
comfort and accuracy,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:19.440
we continue to use camera system
and overcome the low resolution

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.510
issue by using the shirt
color as a temporary identity

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.590
of user.

00:01:25.590 --> 00:01:31.170
My project start with using
OpenPose to track a human,

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:33.330
and then get their joints.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.270
Then we use their joints--
the shoulder and elbow--

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:38.730
to extract the shirt.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.960
As you can see in here,
that we draw the polygon.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:46.860
Then we find all
possible identification

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.580
of people across
multiple camera.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.440
Then we compute [? errors ?]
for each matched shirt

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.640
to be able to obtain
the best prediction.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.120
At the end, we are
able to get around 93%

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:09.539
average accuracy with
this main improvement.

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:16.080
We also acknowledge that we use
shirt as a short-term identity.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.490
This will allow us to
achieve real-time speed.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:24.810
But in the future, we
will integrate this system

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:29.250
with other high accuracy,
but maybe slower,

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.670
and use heavyweight computation
like machine learning

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.120
to fill in the gap between
the short translation

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:42.390
when people no longer wear
the same shirt during the day.

